 *
 * Kept raw: 0x20..0x7e except '"' and '\'. That means '/', '<', '>' and '&'
 * are *not* escaped. Everything else is escaped — the five short forms
 * (\b \t \n \f \r), and \uXXXX with lowercase hex for every other code unit,
 * including 0x7f (DEL) and every code unit above it. Because the loop walks
 * UTF-16 code units, an astral character naturally comes out as its surrogate
 * pair, e.g. U+1F600 -> 😀.
